riscv: dts: sophgo: sg2000: milkv-duos: add on-board eMMC

Add and enable the CV181x eMMC controller (mmc@4300000) on the Milk-V
Duo S. This third MMC instance exists on the SG2000/CV181x family but
not on the plain CV1800B, so the shared cv18xx.dtsi -- which the Duo S
board file inherits from the 64 MiB Duo via cv1800b.dtsi -- does not
describe it. Add it in the board file, the only Duo-family board that
populates eMMC.

The in-tree sdhci-of-dwcmshc driver already bound to the microSD
(compatible sophgo,cv1800b-dwcmshc) drives this controller too and does
all PHY tuning in-kernel. The Duo S wires four data lines to a
non-removable eMMC with a hardware reset line; the VDDIO_SD0_EMMC rail
is shared with the 3.3 V microSD, so eMMC I/O is fixed 3.3 V -- high
speed only, no HS200/HS400. The eMMC enumerates as mmc1 -> /dev/mmcblk1,
leaving the microSD rootfs on mmcblk0 untouched.

Because the board boots from the microSD, the eMMC pads are never
configured: the vendor FSBL only runs its emmc_pad_setting() in the
eMMC-boot path, and the reused milkv_duo U-Boot never touches eMMC. The
eMMC CMD/DAT pads are open-drain (TRM "18OD33"), so left floating the
card never answers CMD1 ("mmc1: Failed to initialize a non-removable
card"). This 6.12 target ships no pinctrl at all, so instantiate the
SG2000 pin controller and add an eMMC pin group replicating the FSBL:
mux the pads to eMMC (function 0), pull-up on CMD/DAT/RSTN, pull-down on
CLK, at 3.3 V. The pinctrl driver writes no mux at probe -- only the
eMMC pins referenced here are touched, so the FSBL-configured microSD /
UART / Ethernet / USB pads are left untouched.

Needs CONFIG_PINCTRL_SOPHGO_SG2000 (selects PINCTRL_SOPHGO_CV18XX).

Signed-off-by: d622 <300083818+d622-au@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
index eeeeeee..fffffff 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-milkv-duos.dts
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 /dts-v1/;
 
 #include "cv1800b.dtsi"
+#include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/pinctrl-sg2000.h>
 
 / {
 	model = "Milk-V Duo S";
@@ -69,3 +70,64 @@
 	dr_mode = "host";
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * On-board 8 GiB eMMC on the CV181x-only third MMC controller, which the
+ * shared cv18xx.dtsi (from the CV1800B, that lacks it) does not describe.
+ * Driven by the same in-tree sophgo,cv1800b-dwcmshc driver as the microSD,
+ * with all PHY tuning done in-kernel.
+ *
+ * Because we boot from the microSD, neither the FSBL (which only configures
+ * the eMMC pads in its eMMC-boot path) nor U-Boot ever sets up the eMMC
+ * pins. The eMMC CMD/DAT pads are open-drain (TRM "18OD33"), so without
+ * pull-ups they float and the card never answers CMD1 ("Failed to
+ * initialize a non-removable card"). This 6.12 target carries no pinctrl
+ * at all, so we instantiate the SG2000 pin controller and add an eMMC pin
+ * group here, replicating the vendor FSBL emmc_pad_setting(): mux the pads
+ * to eMMC (function 0), pull-up on CMD/DAT/RSTN, pull-down on CLK. The
+ * VDDIO_SD0_EMMC rail is shared with the (3.3 V) microSD, so eMMC I/O is
+ * fixed 3.3 V -- high speed only, no HS200 (which needs 1.8 V).
+ */
+&{/soc} {
+	pinctrl@3001000 {
+		compatible = "sophgo,sg2000-pinctrl";
+		reg = <0x03001000 0x1000>,
+		      <0x05027000 0x1000>;
+		reg-names = "sys", "rtc";
+
+		emmc_pins: emmc-pins {
+			emmc-clk-pins {
+				pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_EMMC_CLK, 0)>;
+				bias-pull-down;
+				power-source = <3300>;
+			};
+
+			emmc-cmd-data-pins {
+				pinmux = <PINMUX(PIN_EMMC_CMD, 0)>,
+					 <PINMUX(PIN_EMMC_DAT0, 0)>,
+					 <PINMUX(PIN_EMMC_DAT1, 0)>,
+					 <PINMUX(PIN_EMMC_DAT2, 0)>,
+					 <PINMUX(PIN_EMMC_DAT3, 0)>,
+					 <PINMUX(PIN_EMMC_RSTN, 0)>;
+				bias-pull-up;
+				power-source = <3300>;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+
+	emmc: mmc@4300000 {
+		compatible = "sophgo,cv1800b-dwcmshc";
+		reg = <0x4300000 0x1000>;
+		interrupts = <34 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		clocks = <&clk CLK_AXI4_EMMC>, <&clk CLK_EMMC>;
+		clock-names = "core", "bus";
+		bus-width = <4>;
+		non-removable;
+		no-sd;
+		no-sdio;
+		cap-mmc-hw-reset;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&emmc_pins>;
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+};
